{"version" 2 "boxes" [{"id" "pt_renderer" "properties" {"children" #{#afield/box "pt_tracer"} "parents" #{#afield/box "root"} "name" "path tracing renderer" "_tombstone" false "frame" #afield/rect [40.0 40.0 340.0 110.0] "code" #afield/file-inline {"path" "pt_renderer_code_.kt" "inline" "// The window and the Vulkan renderer every other box in this document inherits.\n// `once.renderer` means re-running this box does not build a second window.\nimport afield.graphics.vulkan.util.Options\nprop<Window>(window)\nprop<Renderer>(renderer)\nOptions.enableHDR = false\nonce.renderer {\n    window = Window(\"Field · Path tracer instrument\")\n    Renderer(window)\n}\nstart(renderer::run)\n"} "preamble" "" "nested" #{}}} {"id" "pt_tracer" "properties" {"children" #{#afield/box "pt_instrument" #afield/box "pt_plot" #afield/box "pt_swap" #afield/box "pt_restore"} "parents" #{#afield/box "root" #afield/box "pt_renderer"} "name" "1 - The tracer, with a log" "_tombstone" false "frame" #afield/rect [40.0 180.0 480.0 142.0] "code" #afield/file-inline {"path" "pt_tracer_code_.kt" "inline" "// The shipped materials scene at 640x360, plus the one new line: a convergence log.\n//\n// `recordConvergence()` attaches a log the tracer appends to from inside its own `render`, so\n// it costs no frames. This replaces the shape four scratch boxes were written in last night --\n// `frames { repeat(180) { frame() } }` with a `println` inside -- which spends 180 real frames\n// to learn what the log already knows.\nimport afield.graphics.scene.fabricated.*\nimport java.io.File\n\nprop<PathTracingRenderer>(tracer)\nprop<PathTraceConvergence>(log)\n\ntracer = PathTraceDemo.install(renderer,\n    File(\"public/docs/assets/fabricate_demo/venice_sunset_1k.exr\").absolutePath)\ntracer.samplesPerFrame = 1\ntracer.maxBounces = 5\ntracer.indirectClamp = 10f\ntracer.exposure = 1.5f\ntracer.blitToScreen()\n\nlog = tracer.recordConvergence()\nprintln(\"${tracer.backend}: ${tracer.triangleCount} triangles, ${tracer.width} x ${tracer.height}\")\n"} "preamble" "" "nested" #{}}} {"id" "pt_instrument" "properties" {"children" #{} "parents" #{#afield/box "root" #afield/box "pt_tracer"} "name" "2 - The instrument, in one line" "_tombstone" false "frame" #afield/rect [40.0 360.0 480.0 142.0] "code" #afield/file-inline {"path" "pt_instrument_code_.kt" "inline" "/*\nRe-run to inspect the live tracer, including its accumulation generation.\nThe up row appears when the declared camera up differs from the effective\nright × forward basis used to make the image.\n*/\nimport afield.graphics.scene.fabricated.PathTracingRenderer\n\nprop<PathTracingRenderer>(tracer)\ndisplay(\"output\", tracer)\n"} "preamble" "" "nested" #{}}} {"id" "pt_plot" "properties" {"children" #{} "parents" #{#afield/box "root" #afield/box "pt_tracer"} "name" "3 - The convergence curve" "_tombstone" false "frame" #afield/rect [800.0 360.0 480.0 142.0] "code" #afield/file-inline {"path" "pt_plot_code_.kt" "inline" "// Samples against wall seconds, with labelled rules where accumulation restarted.\n// Run the swap or restore box, then re-run this convergence box to see the reset.\nimport afield.graphics.scene.fabricated.*\n\nprop<PathTracingRenderer>(tracer)\nprop<PathTraceConvergence>(log)\n\nprintln(log)\nprintln(\"resets so far: \" + log.resetMarks())\nshowConvergence(log)\n"} "preamble" "" "nested" #{}}} {"id" "pt_swap" "properties" {"children" #{} "parents" #{#afield/box "root" #afield/box "pt_tracer"} "name" "4 - Swap the integrator, live" "_tombstone" false "frame" #afield/rect [40.0 680.0 480.0 142.0] "code" #afield/file-inline {"path" "pt_swap_code_.kt" "inline" "// Three calls, three different answers, and that is the whole point of the type.\nimport afield.graphics.scene.fabricated.*\n\nprop<PathTracingRenderer>(tracer)\n\n// 1. No argument offers the packaged integrator -- which is exactly what is already\n//    running. UNCHANGED. `ComputeModulePointer.reload` answers a bare `false` here, the\n//    same `false` it answers for a compile failure, so a `check(...)` around it throws on\n//    a no-op. That is why this returns three outcomes instead of a boolean.\nprintln(tracer.reloadIntegrator())\n\n// 2. A source that does not compile. FAILED, with the compiler's own messages, and the\n//    last working pipeline keeps rendering -- watch the window: the image does not blink.\nprintln(tracer.reloadIntegrator(\"#version 460\\nvoid main() { this is not glsl }\"))\n\n// 3. A real swap, and a deliberately unphysical one: multiply the direct and indirect\n//    terms where the integrator adds them, scale, and curve the result. One line changes,\n//    but the whole ~30 KB integrator is recompiled and hot-swapped under a running camera.\n//    `integratorSource()` hands you the packaged source with this device's HARDWARE_QUERY\n//    define already applied -- the step that used to exist only at two private call sites,\n//    in no document and no API.\n//\n//    This is the line to play with. `radiance` is what reached the camera directly and\n//    `indirect` is what arrived by a bounce; both are vec3 and both are in scope at the end\n//    of the integrator, so anything you can write over the two of them compiles and is in\n//    the window about a second later.\nval remix = tracer.integratorSource()\n    .replace(\"return vec4(radiance+indirect,1);\",\n        \"return vec4(pow(radiance*indirect*2, vec3(0.76)),1);\")\nprintln(tracer.reloadIntegrator(remix))\n\n// Anything the camera sees with no bounce behind it multiplies to zero, so the sunset\n// environment drops to black and the three spheres become the only lit things in the frame,\n// each keeping its own colour over a soft pool on the floor; the gold one holds just its sun\n// glint. The camera has not moved by a single bit.\nprintln(\"reset: '\" + tracer.lastResetReason + \"' generation=\" + tracer.resetGeneration)\n"} "preamble" "" "nested" #{}}} {"id" "pt_restore" "properties" {"children" #{} "parents" #{#afield/box "root" #afield/box "pt_tracer"} "name" "5 - Put the integrator back" "_tombstone" false "frame" #afield/rect [40.0 1020.0 480.0 142.0] "code" #afield/file-inline {"path" "pt_restore_code_.kt" "inline" "// Restore the packaged integrator after the swap box changes the live pipeline.\n// The scene, camera and accumulation buffers are reused.\nimport afield.graphics.scene.fabricated.*\n\nprop<PathTracingRenderer>(tracer)\n\nprintln(tracer.reloadIntegrator())\nprintln(\"reset: '\" + tracer.lastResetReason + \"' generation=\" + tracer.resetGeneration)\n\n// And the instrument again, so you can read the generation count going up and the reason\n// changing. Re-run the convergence box to see the reset as a labelled rule.\ndisplay(\"output\", tracer)\n"} "preamble" "" "nested" #{}}}] "persistentProperties" ["frame" "name" "code" "code_language" "contents_language" "default_property" "file_proxy_mode" "file_proxy_path" "file_proxy_original_path" "file_proxy_mime" "filename" "preamble" "introduction" "attic" "notes" "fragment" "stackSL" "msl" "vertex" "vertex_fragment" "task" "mesh" "raygen" "miss" "closesthit" "anyhit" "intersection" "callable" "fragment_s" "vertex_s" "task_s" "mesh_s" "raygen_s" "miss_s" "closesthit_s" "anyhit_s" "intersection_s" "callable_s" "children" "parents" "compute" "compute_s" "customization" "source_id" "templateId" "_tombstone" "isRemoteJSRoot" "isPythonRoot" ".*_editorState" "metadata" "nested" "nestedIn" "playlist" "pauseList" "bookmarks" "slideShow" "autorun" "layers" "layerFrames" "_controlGroupValues" "ai4_auto_name" "ai4_auto_name_signature" "fileManagerAccessHistory" "isClojureRoot" "isDatalogRoot" "isForthRoot" "isFieldMLRoot" "isMorphoRoot" "isNanoRoot" "nanoLaunchDelayMs" "nanoMemoryInit" "isKotlinJsRoot" "mainLanguage" "spreadsheet"]}